review_notes:
I read the whole proof of `exterior_arc_polygonal_replacement` (lines 10–61). I also read the statements of the lemmas it uses: `exists_finite_disk_collar` (FiniteDiskCollar.lean), `path_near_endpoints` (PathEndpointNeighborhoods.lean) and `polygonal_replacement_with_spurs` (PolygonalBoundaryReplacement.lean). I checked the Mathlib lemmas `Set.insert_subset` and `Set.inter_subset_left` before suggesting them.

Most of the proof is already a direct, well-structured sequence of steps:
- obtain the two collars and the times u, v;
- build the left segment, the middle subarc and the right segment, and show each lies in O;
- concatenate them;
- apply the spur-replacement lemma;
- widen the result back to U.

I considered rewriting `hA`/`hB` (lines 42–52) as one-line terms built from `hspurA.trans`. I did not flag this, because the explicit case split on `a`/`b` versus the exterior is easier to read than a compressed `Or.elim` term. `hright` and `hη` are already short and clear.

There is one justified simplification. The membership facts `a ∈ U` and `b ∈ U` are each re-derived twice with `simpa using hγU 0/1`, and `hSU` proves the subset fact through a case split on elements. I have not compiled the proposed replacement.
